@* The connection's verification state, as a badge. One component, so the Settings page
   and the enrichment pages cannot disagree about what "unverified" looks like. Renders
   nothing when there is no connection at all: the enrichment flow already refuses in
   words and names Settings as the fix.

   This title is the *durable* half of the unverified statement, and the wording has to be
   true on its own terms. The note in _Unverified.cshtml is per-response and vanishes on
   reload; the enrichment pages carry only this. It used to say "Enrichment can still work —
   the endpoint may simply not offer a model list", which is false for a base URL that
   already carried a version segment: the completion then posts to
   /v1/v1/chat/completions, 404s, and no nutrient row is ever written. So it now names three
   of the causes that all look the same here, and promises none of them, in the same order
   the note names them.
   The hover-only reach of a `title` is a real accessibility gap and is recorded as an open
   entry rather than fixed here: whether the sentence becomes visible text or an announced
   accessible name is a design decision (a DESIGN.md amendment), and this copy change
   settles nothing about it. The e2e pins the attribute's text on the enrichment page,
   where a user actually reads it. *@
@model VitaTrack.Web.Models.ConnectionBadgeViewModel
<span class="badge rounded-pill @(Model.Verified ? "bg-success" : "bg-warning text-dark")"
      title="@(Model.Verified
          ? "Your service answered the model-list test with this key."
          : "Your service has not answered the model-list test with this key. The connection is saved but unconfirmed — an endpoint with no model list, a base URL it does not serve, and a rejected key all look the same here.")">
    @(Model.Verified ? "verified" : "unverified")
</span>
